00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.058
That was a couple of years ago.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've had an
interesting couple years.

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.463 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yeah, it's been-
- Haven't ya?

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.031 line:0%
- Yeah, it has been an
interesting couple years.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
I, by the grace of God, I
probably should not be here,

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.670 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
'cause last year,
Memorial Day weekend,

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.472
I had an accident
on my motorcycle,

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:48.341
75 miles an hour on
a interstate highway.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.743
And you know, the fact
that I'm still alive

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.378
is very, very great.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.914
And so it's a pleasure to be
here with you and everything.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:59.586 align:start position:0%
And I'm down here in Livingston,
Texas, at VFW Post 8568.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.255
And I love coming, you know,
getting out of the big cities,

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.591 align:start size:84% position:16%
and getting down to
the small rural areas,

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.359 align:start size:84% position:16%
and especially
being with veterans.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.428
What a great thing
to do, as you know,

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:11.331 align:start size:84% position:16%
as we go into the
holiday season also.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:13.967
- Yeah, and you guys do some
tremendous work with veterans.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.568 align:start size:97% position:3%
Before we get into
everything you're doing now,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.871
and why you're running
for governor of Texas,

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.139
and everything else,

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:22.108
can we just do the
quick two-minute bio

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:25.311
on you and your story, your
service, that sort of thing,

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.547 align:start size:81% position:19%
just so those that
don't know you,

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.315
will fully know you, and
then we'll go from there.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.583
- Well, I gotta tell you,

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.318
when you think about
the American dream,

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.420 align:start size:84% position:16%
and everything
that America offers

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.588
to each and every one of us,

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.323 align:start size:84% position:16%
I call it the equality
of opportunity,

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.125
and not equality of outcomes.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.293
You know, 60 years ago,

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.028 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was born in a
blacks-only hospital,

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.596 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the inner city
of Atlanta, Georgia.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.231
I grew up in the
same neighborhood

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:48.935 align:start size:97% position:3%
that gave us Dr. Martin Luther
King Jr. there in Atlanta.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:52.005 align:start size:81% position:19%
My dad was a World
War II corporal

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.306
in the United States Army,

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.575
and he served this
country at a time

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:59.412
when he was not seen equal to
everyone in a segregated Army.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.981
My mother did 25 years
plus civilian service

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.083 align:start size:88% position:13%
with the Marine
headquarters in Atlanta.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:07.687 align:start size:97% position:3%
My older brother was an
infantryman in Marine Corps,

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.189
and was wounded in Vietnam.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.424 align:start size:84% position:16%
At the age of 15,
my dad challenged me

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.493 align:start size:84% position:16%
to be the first
officer in our family.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.662
And on 31, July, 1982,

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.263
I was commissioned as
a Second Lieutenant

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.898
at the University of Tennessee.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.167
I served 22 years
active duty service

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.770
for the United States Army,
as a field artilleryman,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.572
also as a paratrooper.

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:28.708 align:start size:97% position:3%
13 different countries,
three different combat zones.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.510 align:start size:88% position:13%
The story for our family
doesn't end there.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:33.079
My nephew, who is my
older brother's son,

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.715 align:start size:97% position:3%
he is now a Lieutenant Colonel
in the United States Army,

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.183
continuing to serve.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.352
I've been married for 32
years, I have a great wife.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:42.689
She's really the brain
trust of this couple.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:44.290
She has an MBA and a PhD,

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.092
and I met her when she
was a business professor

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.760
at Kansas State University.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.097 align:start size:97% position:3%
We have two daughters,
Aubrey and Austen, 28 and 24.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.333 align:start size:84% position:16%
And six months ago,
we became grandparents

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:55.802
to an incredible
little grandson,

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.337
by the name of Jaxton Bernard.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:59.072 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that's pretty
much some of my life,

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:01.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, I had a
great opportunity to serve

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:04.677
in the state of Florida as
a United States Congressman.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.480
And back in 2004, I
got the opportunity

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.848
to come back to Texas.

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.084
My last duty sound
was Fort Hood, Texas.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so here I am, now
running to be the governor

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.255
of the state of Texas.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:17.824 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, you definitely handled
the resume question well.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:20.893
So let's talk a little
bit about the states,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.296
'cause you mentioned
the sort of big two,

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.732
or the shining stars, at
least from where I'm at

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.233
at the moment, as you know,

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:30.803
I'm in crazy Los Angeles,
California as we tape this.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.572
But you mentioned Florida,
where you were a Congressman.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.108
You're running for
governor in Texas.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:38.311 align:start size:84% position:16%
Are you sort of
pleased to see the way

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:41.147 align:start size:88% position:13%
the states have gone
in different directions
at this point,

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the federalist
system is sort of working

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.418 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you see hubs of freedom,
like Florida and Texas,

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:46.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I'll throw
Tennessee in there,

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.154
and a couple other states,

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:51.524
while you watch some of the
blue states kinda crumble?

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:53.993
- Well, the interesting thing is

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:56.796
I think we need to reassert
that sense of federalism,

00:04:56.796 --> 00:05:00.366
and what we see as far
as that understanding

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.168 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the 10th Amendment,
where it says

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:04.971 align:start position:0%
that those powers not delegated
to the federal government

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
are reserved to the
states and to the people.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:09.676
And that's where we have a
huge constitutional crisis

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:11.177
here in the state of Texas,

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.980 align:start size:97% position:3%
because Article IV, Section
4 of the Constitution,

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.481
there are two things that
the federal government

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:17.617
is supposed to guarantee to
every state in the union.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.752 align:start size:88% position:13%
Number one, a republican
form of government,

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:22.689 align:start size:97% position:3%
not Republican Party, but
republican form of government.

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:24.223 align:start size:88% position:13%
And number two, they're
supposed to protect

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.725
every state from invasion.

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.226
Well, when you have
an administration,

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:28.895
like we see with the
Biden administration,

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:31.497 align:start size:88% position:13%
that has abdicated their
constitutional duty

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.334 align:start size:97% position:3%
and responsibility to protect
the sovereignty of Texas,

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.502
and the sovereignty of the
United States of America,

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:40.807 align:start size:97% position:3%
Texas has a 1,254 mile border
with a foreign country.

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:43.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it is not just an
everyday foreign country,

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.211
it's a destabilized
foreign country.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.080
And we see this transnational,

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.716 align:start size:88% position:13%
narco-criminal terrorist
organization, known
as the cartels,

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:51.851 align:start size:84% position:16%
really running things
along our border.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:54.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so the founding fathers
and their brilliance

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:56.122
gave the state the ability

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.623
to be able to protect itself,

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
if the federal government
abdicated that.

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:01.461 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so I think that
that's one of the things

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:04.664 align:start size:97% position:3%
we see here in Texas, and
many of the other red states,

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:08.668
is to once again reassert
that ideal of federalism,

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:11.170
the federal government is
supreme over the states

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.405
by the Supremacy Clause,

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:14.474
but it has to be that
they're doing things

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:16.409
pursuant thereof to
the Constitution.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:17.677
And I will challenge anyone,

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:19.712 align:start size:84% position:16%
when we see this
Biden administration,

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:20.913
they're not doing
too many things

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.749
pursuant to the Constitution.

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:24.250
- Is the border issue,

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.486
you think that's the number
one issue on Texans minds?

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:27.987 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, it's a
little hard to gauge,

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.523
