00:17:15.601 --> 00:17:16.835
I've been saying for a while,

00:17:16.835 --> 00:17:18.470
it's sort of woke
verse everybody.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:22.474 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's our job as
everybody, to kinda figure out

00:17:22.474 --> 00:17:24.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
how we can work together,
how we can disagree,

00:17:24.777 --> 00:17:26.812 align:start size:84% position:16%
and agree to
disagree, et cetera.

00:17:26.812 --> 00:17:29.314 align:start size:84% position:16%
How do you think
that thing can work?

00:17:29.314 --> 00:17:30.949 align:start size:84% position:16%
Or do you think
that thing can work?

00:17:30.949 --> 00:17:32.184
- I do think it can work,

00:17:32.184 --> 00:17:34.453
and it has to be based
upon individual rights,

00:17:34.453 --> 00:17:35.788
freedoms, and liberties.

00:17:35.788 --> 00:17:38.157 align:start size:88% position:13%
And you know, I'll give
you case and point,

00:17:38.157 --> 00:17:40.325
just recently, I was
up in New York City,

00:17:40.325 --> 00:17:43.128
and went out to get
something to eat

00:17:43.128 --> 00:17:45.864 align:start size:84% position:16%
after a Fox interview
and everything.

00:17:45.864 --> 00:17:47.466
And I walked into this diner,

00:17:47.466 --> 00:17:51.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
and guy asked me, "Where's
your COVID shot card?"

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.639 line:0%
And I said, "I don't
have a COVID shot card,

00:17:53.639 --> 00:17:54.840 line:0%
I'm visiting here from Texas."

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.608 line:0%
He said, "Well, you
can't eat here."

00:17:56.608 --> 00:17:59.311 line:0%
I think that's going to be
the thing that unites people,

00:17:59.311 --> 00:18:01.680
because I remember
my mother and father,

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.015
once upon a time, they were told

00:18:03.015 --> 00:18:04.550 align:start size:84% position:16%
that they couldn't
eat in certain places,

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:06.085
because of their skin color.

00:18:06.085 --> 00:18:08.387
But now we're being told that
we can't eat in certain places

00:18:08.387 --> 00:18:09.855
because someone has decided

00:18:09.855 --> 00:18:12.091 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we have to get this thing
injected into our bodies.

00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:14.626
And I really believe that
when people start to hear

00:18:14.626 --> 00:18:18.063 align:start size:97% position:3%
that they no longer have
control over their own bodies,

00:18:18.063 --> 00:18:19.565 align:start size:81% position:19%
that's going to
be a rallying cry.

00:18:19.565 --> 00:18:22.134
Just the same as you've
seen when Terry McAuliffe

00:18:22.134 --> 00:18:23.469
stands up in a debate and says,

00:18:23.469 --> 00:18:25.204
"Parents don't have
a right to decide

00:18:25.204 --> 00:18:26.972
what their children
are being taught."

00:18:26.972 --> 00:18:29.641 align:start size:84% position:16%
Oh man, you brought
out people in Virginia

00:18:29.641 --> 00:18:30.876
that would have never cared

00:18:30.876 --> 00:18:32.945
about a Virginia
gubernatorial race.

00:18:32.945 --> 00:18:36.148 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so a year ago, Joe
Biden wins Virginia

00:18:36.148 --> 00:18:37.783
by 11 or 12 points.

00:18:37.783 --> 00:18:41.653 align:start position:0%
A year later, they lose
Virginia by two or three points.

00:18:41.653 --> 00:18:43.856
So I think that that's the
shift that we see happening,

00:18:43.856 --> 00:18:46.291 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you start to touch
people's individual rights,

00:18:46.291 --> 00:18:47.493
freedom, and liberty,

00:18:47.493 --> 00:18:49.428 align:start size:88% position:13%
when you start to reach
inside their homes,

00:18:49.428 --> 00:18:50.796
or affect their bodies,

00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:52.564 align:start size:84% position:16%
then people are gonna
wake up to this.

00:18:52.564 --> 00:18:54.666
- Yeah, it used to be
my body, my choice.

00:18:54.666 --> 00:18:56.335
Not so much for them anymore.

00:18:56.335 --> 00:18:58.904 align:start size:84% position:16%
But you mentioned
two to three points.

00:18:58.904 --> 00:19:00.239
Speaking of two to three points,

00:19:00.239 --> 00:19:04.843
the last senatorial
campaign in Texas,

00:19:04.843 --> 00:19:09.281
Ted Cruz only beat Beto
by about three points.

00:19:09.281 --> 00:19:10.916
I think it was 2 1/2,
if I'm not mistaken.

00:19:10.916 --> 00:19:12.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was a lot closer.
- Yeah, 2 1/2.

00:19:12.317 --> 00:19:14.553 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, it was a lot
closer than people thought.

00:19:14.553 --> 00:19:16.855
What does that tell you about
what's happening in Texas?

00:19:16.855 --> 00:19:20.626 align:start position:0%
Is Austin getting weird
filtering throughout the state?

00:19:20.626 --> 00:19:22.227
Is that what's happening?

00:19:22.227 --> 00:19:24.596 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I think
that the Beto effect

00:19:24.596 --> 00:19:28.500
that happened in 2018 was
that he was a new person,

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:31.103
and the media built
this aura around him.

00:19:31.103 --> 00:19:32.971
And there was a lot
of angst and anxiety

00:19:32.971 --> 00:19:34.439
against Senator Cruz.

00:19:34.439 --> 00:19:36.275
But now the cat's out the bag,

00:19:36.275 --> 00:19:39.178 align:start position:0%
and we know who this Mr O'Rourke
is, and what he stands for.

00:19:39.178 --> 00:19:40.812
And he's completely antithetical

00:19:40.812 --> 00:19:42.681
to Texas principles and values.

00:19:42.681 --> 00:19:44.783
But when you look at what
has happened in Texas,

00:19:44.783 --> 00:19:47.719 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you look at what has
happened in many red states,

00:19:47.719 --> 00:19:49.655 align:start size:81% position:19%
California used
to be a red state.

00:19:49.655 --> 00:19:51.657
I mean, this was the state
that gave us Richard Nixon,

00:19:51.657 --> 00:19:53.258
and Ronald Reagan.

00:19:53.258 --> 00:19:56.228
What has happening in Texas
is that we have had governors

00:19:56.228 --> 00:19:57.663
going to blue states,

00:19:57.663 --> 00:19:59.798 align:start position:0%
and saying, "Why don't you
pick up and move your business,

00:19:59.798 --> 00:20:01.700
or your corporation here,

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:03.101
because we have better policies,

00:20:03.101 --> 00:20:05.103 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you can
economically thrive."

00:20:05.103 --> 00:20:06.638
But the thing that is happening

00:20:06.638 --> 00:20:09.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that as they bring
this workforce with them,

00:20:09.041 --> 00:20:12.511
no one is talking to them
saying, "Don't screw it up

00:20:12.511 --> 00:20:14.213 align:start size:84% position:16%
when you move to this
new place, okay?"

00:20:14.213 --> 00:20:16.582 align:start size:84% position:16%
I can leave California
Silicon Valley,

00:20:16.582 --> 00:20:18.217
because this place sucks.

00:20:18.217 --> 00:20:20.018
And so they ended
up coming here,

00:20:20.018 --> 00:20:21.520 align:start size:81% position:19%
and they wanna
vote the same way.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:24.389 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now there are individuals
that are leaving California,

00:20:24.389 --> 00:20:25.657 align:start size:84% position:16%
Illinois, New York,
and New Jersey,

00:20:25.657 --> 00:20:27.125
for all the right reasons.

00:20:27.125 --> 00:20:30.195 align:start size:84% position:16%
But when you have
this mass transplant,

00:20:30.195 --> 00:20:31.997
and I call it the locust effect.

00:20:31.997 --> 00:20:34.600 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, people go to
the very good, thriving,

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:36.268
fertile grounds like
California used to be,

00:20:36.268 --> 00:20:37.836
and they chew it
up and destroy it.

00:20:37.836 --> 00:20:39.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they look and see
where else they can go.

00:20:39.972 --> 00:20:42.574
But I will tell you,
hats off to Elon Musk,

00:20:42.574 --> 00:20:44.343
because earlier in November,

00:20:44.343 --> 00:20:47.279
Elon Musk put out a tweet to
the people there in Austin,

00:20:47.279 --> 00:20:48.847
saying, admonishing them,

00:20:48.847 --> 00:20:52.150 align:start size:97% position:3%
saying, "Don't let Austin
become the new San Francisco,"

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:54.253
because the people in Austin,

00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:55.487
since they defunded the police,

00:20:55.487 --> 00:20:57.489 align:start size:84% position:16%
got all woke and
everything like that,

00:20:57.489 --> 00:21:00.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
they've seen a 66%
increase in violent crime,

00:21:00.192 --> 00:21:02.728
71% increase in homicide.

00:21:02.728 --> 00:21:05.430 align:start size:97% position:3%
The homeless situation there
is absolutely disgusting

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:08.300
and appalling, people don't go
downtown in Austin at night.

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:10.802 align:start size:88% position:13%
But yet they still
voted down a proposition

00:21:10.802 --> 00:21:12.337
to re-fund the police.

00:21:12.337 --> 00:21:14.640 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so I think
that's, at the core,

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.541
something that's
going to change,

00:21:16.541 --> 00:21:17.776
because all of a sudden,

00:21:17.776 --> 00:21:19.344 align:start size:88% position:13%
when people realize that
their personal safety

00:21:19.344 --> 00:21:22.381 align:start size:97% position:3%
and security is at risk,
they'll back away from this.

00:21:22.381 --> 00:21:24.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Can you get those
people though, to change?

00:21:24.783 --> 00:21:27.486 align:start size:97% position:3%
I get that you might be
able to get the true Texan,

00:21:27.486 --> 00:21:29.588
that's been there
for a lifetime,

00:21:29.588 --> 00:21:32.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go, "Okay, we really
gotta vote the right way."

00:21:32.457 --> 00:21:34.126
But the ones that come
from Silicon Valley,

00:21:34.126 --> 00:21:36.428 align:start size:84% position:16%
it takes sort of a
little smacking around

00:21:36.428 --> 00:21:38.030
for them to realize
that they're leaving

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:39.965
the thing that they voted for.

00:21:39.965 --> 00:21:41.233 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It does, and I think
it's another thing

00:21:41.233 --> 00:21:43.168
that we have to do
is teach them about

00:21:43.168 --> 00:21:46.371
the history of Texas, or
the history of Georgia,

00:21:46.371 --> 00:21:48.974
or Tennessee, and why
they're successful.

00:21:48.974 --> 00:21:51.576
And understand that Texas is
the only state in the union

00:21:51.576 --> 00:21:54.246 align:start size:97% position:3%
that fought for and won
its independence by itself.

00:21:54.246 --> 00:21:56.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think the other
thing that we have to do,

00:21:56.615 --> 00:21:59.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
without a doubt, is
understand that, you know,

00:21:59.251 --> 00:22:01.453
find out where those
strong crossing points,

00:22:01.453 --> 00:22:03.055
like you and I just discussed,

00:22:03.055 --> 00:22:05.290
where you get the 60 to 65%.

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:08.260 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because I think
it's that 35 to 40%,

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:10.796
you're probably just not
gonna get through to them.

00:22:10.796 --> 00:22:12.931
But let's go after the
people that understand,

00:22:12.931 --> 00:22:14.866
and that's why we
had such success

00:22:14.866 --> 00:22:16.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
when I was the
chairman of the party,

00:22:16.401 --> 00:22:18.337
going down into the
Rio Grande Valley.

00:22:18.337 --> 00:22:20.238
And we told the people in
the Hispanic community,

00:22:20.238 --> 00:22:23.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
who had never seen a
Republican Party chairman

00:22:23.108 --> 00:22:25.177 align:start size:88% position:13%
in the Rio Grande
Valley previous to that,

00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:28.046 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Your principles and values
are our principles of values."

00:22:28.046 --> 00:22:29.748
You know, it wasn't
about the outreach.

00:22:29.748 --> 00:22:31.283
It was about the engagement.

00:22:31.283 --> 00:22:33.151
Outreach means you show up
at a Black History Month,

00:22:33.151 --> 00:22:35.053
Hispanic American
Heritage Month,

00:22:35.053 --> 00:22:36.355 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then people
never see you again,

00:22:36.355 --> 00:22:38.290 align:start size:88% position:13%
until a couple of months
before an election.

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:41.259
But when you're there all
the time, 24 seven, 365,

00:22:41.259 --> 00:22:45.797 align:start position:0%
talking about those common
points that you can expand upon,

00:22:45.797 --> 00:22:47.566 align:start size:84% position:16%
then people will
rally to your cause.

00:22:47.566 --> 00:22:48.867
And then again,
I think that this

00:22:48.867 --> 00:22:51.703 align:start size:97% position:3%
is more of a
philosophical, ideological,

00:22:51.703 --> 00:22:55.207
cultural basis that we
have to approach things,

00:22:55.207 --> 00:22:57.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not just about
political parties anymore.

00:22:57.909 --> 00:23:01.146 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So I hate to do the identity
politics thing, obviously,

00:23:01.146 --> 00:23:02.714
and I know you don't
want to do it either,

00:23:02.714 --> 00:23:05.751
but it exists, whether
we talk about it or not.

00:23:05.751 --> 00:23:07.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, that's
their battleground.

00:23:07.352 --> 00:23:08.754
- That's what they've got.

00:23:08.754 --> 00:23:11.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
As you know, I campaigned
with Larry Elder,

00:23:11.156 --> 00:23:12.691
who's a good friend of mine.

00:23:12.691 --> 00:23:14.826 align:start size:84% position:16%
I saw what the
machine did to him,

00:23:14.826 --> 00:23:17.963
for Joe Biden to show up here
the day before the election,

00:23:17.963 --> 00:23:21.466
refused to say Larry's name,
call him, "A Trump clone,"

00:23:21.466 --> 00:23:24.102
a guy who grew up in South
Central LA, son of a janitor.

00:23:24.102 --> 00:23:25.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, it's so
extraordinarily evil,

00:23:25.871 --> 00:23:27.272
the stuff that Gavin Newsom did,

00:23:27.272 --> 00:23:29.608
the evil ads that Reed
Hastings from Netflix

00:23:29.608 --> 00:23:31.143
put out about Larry,

00:23:31.143 --> 00:23:33.845 align:start position:0%
"Black face of white supremacy,"
according to "LA Times,"

00:23:33.845 --> 00:23:35.680
you know all this stuff,

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:37.516
there's obviously gonna
be a version of that

00:23:37.516 --> 00:23:39.484
that's going to come after you.

00:23:39.484 --> 00:23:41.219
You've been through
the game before,

00:23:41.219 --> 00:23:44.222
but are you ready for it,
in a gubernatorial thing,

00:23:44.222 --> 00:23:45.924 align:start size:88% position:13%
which is different than
congressional race,

00:23:45.924 --> 00:23:49.261 align:start size:88% position:13%
and being a talking
head on Fox, et cetera?

00:23:49.261 --> 00:23:50.962
- Well, absolutely,
and one of the things

00:23:50.962 --> 00:23:52.798
about being here in
the state of Texas,

00:23:52.798 --> 00:23:54.733
the Republican Party
of Texas was founded

00:23:54.733 --> 00:23:56.635
on Independence Day of 1867,

00:23:56.635 --> 00:24:00.071
by 150 black men
in Houston, Texas.

00:24:00.071 --> 00:24:02.707
One of the early chairman
was Norris Wright Cuney.

00:24:02.707 --> 00:24:04.176
You think about Juneteenth,

00:24:04.176 --> 00:24:06.077
and you think about how recently

00:24:06.077 --> 00:24:07.712
they just dedicated a statue

00:24:07.712 --> 00:24:09.748
to a man who was a former slave,

00:24:09.748 --> 00:24:11.416
State Senator Matthew Gaines,

00:24:11.416 --> 00:24:14.586 align:start size:84% position:16%
who was instrumental
in establishing
Texas A&amp;M University,

00:24:14.586 --> 00:24:16.521
and Prairie View A&amp;M University.

00:24:16.521 --> 00:24:19.057 align:start size:88% position:13%
And he's buried there
at Texas A&amp;M University.

00:24:19.057 --> 00:24:20.592
Guess who's also buried there,

00:24:20.592 --> 00:24:22.260
on the campus of Texas A&amp;M?

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:25.397
You know, President George
H. W. Bush and his wife.

00:24:25.397 --> 00:24:27.566
And so when you talk
about these things,

00:24:27.566 --> 00:24:30.602
and you use history
to illuminate people,

00:24:30.602 --> 00:24:32.337 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you just talk
about the real party

00:24:32.337 --> 00:24:35.073
of systemic racism, has
been the Democrat Party.

00:24:35.073 --> 00:24:37.108
I often tell folks,
"There are two ways

00:24:37.108 --> 00:24:38.910
that you can enslave people.

00:24:38.910 --> 00:24:41.112 align:start size:84% position:16%
One is that you work
them for no pay.

00:24:41.112 --> 00:24:43.648
And the other is that you
pay them for no work."

00:24:43.648 --> 00:24:45.617
And tell me what this
party has done that

00:24:45.617 --> 00:24:47.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the history of the
United States of America?

00:24:47.219 --> 00:24:49.521
So I think that as long
as you stand strong,

00:24:49.521 --> 00:24:52.157 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you always go on the
offense, not on the defense,

00:24:52.157 --> 00:24:54.426
you put them back
on their heels,

00:24:54.426 --> 00:24:57.662
you know, all this talk about
white supremacy and racism.,

00:24:57.662 --> 00:24:59.598
I have yet to see
anyone on the left

00:24:59.598 --> 00:25:01.399
speak out against
Margaret Sanger.

00:25:01.399 --> 00:25:04.769 align:start size:97% position:3%
Margaret Sanger create Planned
Parenthood for one reason,

00:25:04.769 --> 00:25:06.037
because she believed that blacks

00:25:06.037 --> 00:25:07.973
were undesirables
and human weeds.

00:25:07.973 --> 00:25:11.776
And yet we see 71 to 73% of
Planned Parenthood clinics

00:25:11.776 --> 00:25:13.211
in minority communities.

00:25:13.211 --> 00:25:15.480
So as long as we
are the aggressor,

00:25:15.480 --> 00:25:17.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
as long as we are pitting
them on their heels,

00:25:17.649 --> 00:25:19.217 align:start size:84% position:16%
we don't let them
define the narrative.

00:25:19.217 --> 00:25:21.620
And I think that's the thing
that the military taught me,

00:25:21.620 --> 00:25:23.154
and that's how we're
going to make sure

00:25:23.154 --> 00:25:27.025
that we don't allow them to
dictate and define who I am.

00:25:27.025 --> 00:25:28.693 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Are there other
things going on in Texas

00:25:28.693 --> 00:25:30.395
that maybe we're
not hearing about,

00:25:30.395 --> 00:25:32.397
from a national perspective,

00:25:32.397 --> 00:25:33.732
that you guys are aware of,

00:25:33.732 --> 00:25:35.800
or that you think are
the keys to winning,

00:25:35.800 --> 00:25:37.602 align:start size:81% position:19%
and creating a
flourishing state?

00:25:37.602 --> 00:25:39.838 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Oh, sure, without a doubt,
the property tax system

00:25:39.838 --> 00:25:42.007
that we have here, sixth
highest in the country.

00:25:42.007 --> 00:25:44.576
And it's really Marxist,
because here in Texas,

00:25:44.576 --> 00:25:47.012
who would have ever thought
you can pay off your land,

00:25:47.012 --> 00:25:49.347
you can pay off your mortgage,
you can never own your home.

00:25:49.347 --> 00:25:51.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we've got to
transition away from that.

00:25:51.449 --> 00:25:54.619 align:start size:97% position:3%
A lot of people maybe
remember this past February,

00:25:54.619 --> 00:25:57.556
where Texas looked like
North Korea at night,

