00:34:28.399 --> 00:34:30.301 align:start size:88% position:13%
our freedoms and
liberties in our states.

00:34:30.301 --> 00:34:31.969 align:start size:97% position:3%
Remember, in the
Declaration of Independence

00:34:31.969 --> 00:34:34.038
it says, "Free and
independent states

00:34:34.038 --> 00:34:35.973
created these United
States of America,"

00:34:35.973 --> 00:34:38.109
and I think we need to go
back and reassert that.

00:34:38.109 --> 00:34:39.477 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Have states
actually done that?

00:34:39.477 --> 00:34:40.745
I actually don't know.

00:34:40.745 --> 00:34:42.280
They've basically, if
the federal government

00:34:42.280 --> 00:34:44.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
is in dereliction of duty,
they can basically say,

00:34:44.482 --> 00:34:46.784 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Hey, we're just not
gonna pay you that money

00:34:46.784 --> 00:34:48.686 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you've been
collecting from us,"

00:34:48.686 --> 00:34:50.188
or a portion of it or something?

00:34:50.188 --> 00:34:51.556
- I think you're starting
to see some challenges.

00:34:51.556 --> 00:34:53.424
You look at Oklahoma right now,

00:34:53.424 --> 00:34:55.393 align:start size:88% position:13%
they're saying that
they're not gonna allow

00:34:55.393 --> 00:34:56.761 align:start size:84% position:16%
the federal government
to come down,

00:34:56.761 --> 00:34:58.930 align:start size:81% position:19%
and just use their
National Guard.

00:34:58.930 --> 00:35:00.598
And of course there's a
fight going back there.

00:35:00.598 --> 00:35:02.867
And so, but I think that
that's something that we,

00:35:02.867 --> 00:35:04.435 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's about the
power of the purse.

00:35:04.435 --> 00:35:05.870 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think states
need to understand

00:35:05.870 --> 00:35:07.205
that power that they have,

00:35:07.205 --> 00:35:10.141 align:start size:84% position:16%
and start strangling
the resources

00:35:10.141 --> 00:35:12.043
going back to the
federal government.

00:35:12.043 --> 00:35:13.644
Because right now, when you look

00:35:13.644 --> 00:35:15.079
at what the federal government

00:35:15.079 --> 00:35:16.714 align:start size:97% position:3%
is doing with our tax dollars,
you just brought it out,

00:35:16.714 --> 00:35:19.984 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's going to bail out
blue states when they fail.

00:35:19.984 --> 00:35:22.620
And so I don't think that
we want to see that happen.

00:35:22.620 --> 00:35:25.289
- Yeah, what do you do
when you have a state

00:35:25.289 --> 00:35:27.225 align:start size:84% position:16%
that basically is
doing the right stuff?

00:35:27.225 --> 00:35:29.193 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then, you know, we
talked about Austin before,

00:35:29.193 --> 00:35:31.996
there's some backwards
stuff going on there.

00:35:31.996 --> 00:35:33.498
What would you, as governor, do,

00:35:33.498 --> 00:35:36.667
if you sat down with
the mayor of Austin,

00:35:36.667 --> 00:35:39.103
and you felt the policies were
going in the wrong direction?

00:35:39.103 --> 00:35:42.106 align:start size:97% position:3%
When I was there last time,
it wasn't quite San Francisco,

00:35:42.106 --> 00:35:44.008 align:start size:97% position:3%
but there's a lot of homeless,
et cetera, et cetera.

00:35:44.008 --> 00:35:45.276
What do you do as the governor?

00:35:45.276 --> 00:35:47.912
What kind of leverage
do you actually have?

00:35:47.912 --> 00:35:49.180
- Well, I think it's
first and foremost,

00:35:49.180 --> 00:35:50.715 align:start size:84% position:16%
you've gotta educate
the electorate

00:35:50.715 --> 00:35:52.850
that lives within
that municipality,

00:35:52.850 --> 00:35:54.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
and get them to understand
that this is something

00:35:54.652 --> 00:35:56.420
that you can do by petition,

00:35:56.420 --> 00:35:58.189
by referendum and what have you.

00:35:58.189 --> 00:36:01.559 align:start size:84% position:16%
But without a doubt,
my responsibility
is for all Texans.

00:36:01.559 --> 00:36:04.395 align:start size:97% position:3%
And when I see that you have
these district attorneys

00:36:04.395 --> 00:36:06.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are saying, "We're
not gonna prosecute people

00:36:06.564 --> 00:36:10.134
for anything at $750 or less,"

00:36:10.134 --> 00:36:12.069
when you have these
judges here in Texas

00:36:12.069 --> 00:36:14.705 align:start size:97% position:3%
that are releasing criminals
out into the streets,

00:36:14.705 --> 00:36:16.507
you know, when you dig into
the Texas State Constitution,

00:36:16.507 --> 00:36:19.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
you find that the governor
is able to impeach,

00:36:19.410 --> 00:36:22.113 align:start position:0%
or start impeachment proceedings
against these judges.

00:36:22.113 --> 00:36:24.482
You have to work with
the Texas State House,

00:36:24.482 --> 00:36:26.584
but you have to stay
within the rule of law.

00:36:26.584 --> 00:36:28.653
You don't wanna be seen
as some type of dictator,

00:36:28.653 --> 00:36:29.921
or anything like that.

00:36:29.921 --> 00:36:31.489
But you've gotta get
people to understand

00:36:31.489 --> 00:36:33.224
that I will stand up
for the rule of law.

00:36:33.224 --> 00:36:34.759
We'll make sure that
I protect the safety

00:36:34.759 --> 00:36:36.160
and security of individuals,

00:36:36.160 --> 00:36:37.128
but you gotta empower the people

00:36:37.128 --> 00:36:38.863
to be able to do these things.

00:36:38.863 --> 00:36:41.332
And again, I think that you
see an awakening toward that.

00:36:41.332 --> 00:36:44.302
- Do you think conservatives
have to use a little more power

00:36:44.302 --> 00:36:46.804
than they would want to perhaps?

00:36:46.804 --> 00:36:48.773
- Yeah, you know, one of
the things I always say

00:36:48.773 --> 00:36:51.142
is that Republicans
have to stop bringing

00:36:51.142 --> 00:36:53.778
a plastic spoon to a gunfight,

00:36:53.778 --> 00:36:55.680 line:0%
because they always just think,

00:36:55.680 --> 00:36:57.615 line:0%
"Nah, they're not going
to do anything about it."

00:36:57.615 --> 00:36:59.584 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
So we cannot continue
to allow them

00:36:59.584 --> 00:37:00.585 line:0%
to kick sand in our face.

00:37:00.585 --> 00:37:01.852 line:0%
We gotta stand up,

00:37:01.852 --> 00:37:03.221
and I think that's what
people are looking for.

00:37:03.221 --> 00:37:06.424
And so when we make the
case, I mean, we win.

00:37:06.424 --> 00:37:07.858 align:start size:84% position:16%
You look at what
happened in Virginia,

00:37:07.858 --> 00:37:09.927 align:start size:88% position:13%
look what almost
happened in New Jersey.

00:37:09.927 --> 00:37:12.230
The left knows that they're
gonna have an Armageddon,

00:37:12.230 --> 00:37:14.699
a political Armageddon
in the midterm elections,

00:37:14.699 --> 00:37:17.501 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's going to make Barack
Obama look pretty bad.

00:37:17.501 --> 00:37:20.037
I mean, he lost
63 seats in 2010.

00:37:20.037 --> 00:37:22.006
Joe Biden's gonna
lose even more.

00:37:22.006 --> 00:37:23.474
But we have to understand

00:37:23.474 --> 00:37:25.243 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we can't have
the peaks and valleys.

00:37:25.243 --> 00:37:26.744
We have to have a steady state.

00:37:26.744 --> 00:37:29.180
And I tell people that the
most important elections

00:37:29.180 --> 00:37:31.782 align:start size:97% position:3%
are those elections that are
local, the city councils,

00:37:31.782 --> 00:37:35.086
the school boards, the county
commissions, the DA races,

00:37:35.086 --> 00:37:36.954 align:start size:84% position:16%
all of those things
are the closest

00:37:36.954 --> 00:37:39.023 align:start size:84% position:16%
to the individual
citizens down there,

00:37:39.023 --> 00:37:40.791 align:start size:81% position:19%
we gotta start
focusing on those.

00:37:40.791 --> 00:37:42.460 align:start size:84% position:16%
- In our last
couple minutes here,

00:37:42.460 --> 00:37:44.528
what else is on your mind?

00:37:44.528 --> 00:37:46.864 align:start size:84% position:16%
Maybe not purely
political these days,

00:37:46.864 --> 00:37:48.132 align:start size:81% position:19%
I know you're also
a man of faith,

00:37:48.132 --> 00:37:51.269 align:start size:88% position:13%
that frames a lot of
your beliefs, of course.

00:37:51.269 --> 00:37:54.038
What else is on your mind
in this holiday season?

00:37:54.038 --> 00:37:57.908 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, college
football, I love that,

00:37:57.908 --> 00:37:59.410
being brought up down South.

00:37:59.410 --> 00:38:02.513
And so I always get honed
up for college football.

00:38:02.513 --> 00:38:05.549
But without a doubt, I
mean the blessing of life

00:38:05.549 --> 00:38:09.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
that came into our family,
with our new grandson,

00:38:09.053 --> 00:38:11.555
and this'll be his
first Christmas.

00:38:11.555 --> 00:38:15.159
And on December the 1st, we
turned on the house lights,

00:38:15.159 --> 00:38:17.161 align:start size:81% position:19%
and just seeing
his face light up.

00:38:17.161 --> 00:38:20.564 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, we have many
challenges that we have here,

00:38:20.564 --> 00:38:21.899 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we're still
the greatest nation

00:38:21.899 --> 00:38:23.267
that the world has ever known.

00:38:23.267 --> 00:38:24.835
But I think that now's the time,

00:38:24.835 --> 00:38:26.003
when you look at a grandson,

00:38:26.003 --> 00:38:27.471 align:start size:88% position:13%
you look at our children
or grandchildren,

00:38:27.471 --> 00:38:30.041
everyone, just stand up and
fight for what is right,

00:38:30.041 --> 00:38:31.876
and make sure that we are
not the first generation

00:38:31.876 --> 00:38:33.711
that does not pass
on something better

00:38:33.711 --> 00:38:36.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
to subsequent
generations, 'cause again,

00:38:36.681 --> 00:38:37.948
my dad was born in 1920,

00:38:37.948 --> 00:38:41.052
and my mom was born
in 1931 down South.

00:38:41.052 --> 00:38:44.155 align:start size:97% position:3%
And here I am, on a
national televised program,

00:38:44.155 --> 00:38:46.891
talking to you, Dave, that's
what America is all about.

00:38:46.891 --> 00:38:48.492
The equality of opportunity,

00:38:48.492 --> 00:38:50.795 align:start size:84% position:16%
and not the equality
of outcomes.

00:38:50.795 --> 00:38:53.297
- Colonel West, we live in
a time with very few people

00:38:53.297 --> 00:38:56.867 align:start position:0%
who speak as cleanly and
clearly, and honestly as you do,

00:38:56.867 --> 00:38:58.302 align:start size:81% position:19%
so I'm proud to
call you a friend.

00:38:58.302 --> 00:39:00.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
And would you be willing,
would you be willing

00:39:00.237 --> 00:39:02.473 align:start size:84% position:16%
to have a crazy
right-winger like me,

00:39:02.473 --> 00:39:05.843
maybe open for you
on a campaign stop?

00:39:05.843 --> 00:39:06.977 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Absolutely.
- Larry'll show you my resume,

00:39:06.977 --> 00:39:08.779
it's pretty decent.

00:39:08.779 --> 00:39:10.748 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I think your resume
is real decent.

00:39:10.748 --> 00:39:12.850
And I'd love to see
you here in Texas,

00:39:12.850 --> 00:39:15.353 align:start size:84% position:16%
because so goes Texas,
so goes America.

00:39:15.353 --> 00:39:17.722
And so goes America,
so goes the free world.

00:39:17.722 --> 00:39:20.191
So Texas is important
for the free world.

00:39:20.191 --> 00:39:22.560
- Colonel Allen West, I
wish you luck, my friend.

00:39:22.560 --> 00:39:23.994
Merry Christmas to you.

00:39:23.994 --> 00:39:25.496
- Christmas, take care, Dave.

00:39:25.496 --> 00:39:27.098 align:start size:84% position:16%
- If you're looking
for more honest

00:39:27.098 --> 00:39:29.166 align:start size:97% position:3%
and thoughtful conversations
about politics,

00:39:29.166 --> 00:39:30.568
instead of nonstop yelling,

00:39:30.568 --> 00:39:32.503
check out our politics playlist.

